// Date: 2018-03-17 | Modified: 2023-05-16
// ATT&CK: lateral-movement, T1563.002, T1021.001
// Tags: car.2013-07-002
// Description: Detects a suspicious RDP session redirect using tscon.exe
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - http://www.korznikov.com/2017/03/0-day-or-feature-privilege-escalation.html
//   - https://medium.com/@networksecurity/rdp-hijacking-how-to-hijack-rds-and-remoteapp-sessions-transparently-to-move-through-an-da2a1e73a5f6
//   - https://www.hackingarticles.in/rdp-session-hijacking-with-tscon/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_tscon_rdp_redirect.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains " /dest:rdp-tcp#"
